// CBS FA / Harmony FA2 shared 256-byte cartridge RAM.
//
// VCSC exposes mapper-owned cartridge RAM to applications under the common
// named-memory qualifier `cartram`; this file supplies the FA/FA2 window.
// Both schemes decode two adjacent 256-byte ports in the selected 4K cartridge window:
// writes at $F000-$F0FF and reads at $F100-$F1FF. The underlying RAM is shared
// by all ROM banks and survives bank selection. Reset/startup clears BSS and
// copies DATA through the write alias just like Superchip RAM.
// Included by the public FA and FA2 cartridge profiles.

mem cartram { $read_start:0xF100 $write_start:0xF000 $size:0x0100 $rw $read_hazard };
